 winners, 2012–2022\\n2026 winners\\n2025 winners\\nJunior Research Grant\\nMaria Jassinskaja, Lund University, Sweden\\nT\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-b34424f0bb7a7d0dc0752cfc\", \"title\": \"Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3910, \"end\": 4832, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 922}, {\"start\": 5073, \"end\": 5093, \"excerpt_start\": 923, \"excerpt_end\": 943}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Topics-in-Focus program\\nSupport for a changing world.\\nWith advancements in medical technology and research, there’s never been a more exciting time to be involved in hematology.\\nAs pioneers in our field, our role is to lead the change and find novel ways to incorporate new techniques and therapies into daily practice. We need to rapidly deploy these innovations to fuel our advance towards prevention, a cure, and improved quality of life.\\nOverview\\nEHA launched the Topics-in-Focus program to provide support and guidance to hematologists and amplify efforts by focusing on a specific disease related or area related topics to provide better access to innovation.\\nThe program is designed to:\\nRaise awareness\\nProvide education\\nDevelop further research frameworks and access\\nBuild a network of experts in specific focus areas\\nThe program has two strands, each with a specific theme:\\nPrecision hematology\\nHemoglobinopathies\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"title\": \"Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3902, \"end\": 4532, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 630}, {\"start\": 4773, \"end\": 4793, \"excerpt_start\": 631, \"excerpt_end\": 651}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nHemaSphere\\nGrants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-82ed4576ec5ac8372f114a9b\", \"title\": \"EHA2027 Congress - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA2027 Congress - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3882, \"end\": 5254, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1372}, {\"start\": 5495, \"end\": 5515, \"excerpt_start\": 1373, \"excerpt_end\": 1393}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA2027 Congress\\nShape the future of hematology\\nJune 10–13, 2027\\n| Barcelona, Spain\\nLet’s meet at EHA2027, where we connect the global hematology community.\\nEHA2027 will once again offer an exceptional scientific program, featuring a seamless flow of engagement across plenary sessions—including the opening ceremony, plenary abstracts session, and presidential sessions—alongside carefully curated sponsored sessions spread throughout each Congress day.\\nWith a comprehensive program and two poster sessions, we look forward to sharing the latest clinical and research updates in hematology with you.\\nEHA2027 is intended for medical professionals, national hematology societies, patient advocates, medical industry, and media worldwide.\\nThe Congress is not open to the general public.\\nPatient advocates are welcome to attend scientific sessions.\\nKey Dates\\nMarch 1, 2027\\nAbstract submission deadline