3ab6b0c81b9da0eab\", \"url\": \"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fehaweb.org%2Fresearch-innovation%2Fgrants%2Feha-grants-hall-of-fame%2F2025-winners\", \"text\": \"twitter\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 3934, \"end\": 4114, \"text\": \"rs\\nLeft Sidebar\\n11 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\n2023 winners\\n2024 winners\\n2025 winners\\nPrevious winners, 2012–2022\\n2026 winners\\n2025 winners\\nJun\"}}, {\"id\": \"l100\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-cadb8bc3ab6b0c81b9da0eab\", \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fehaweb.org%2Fresearch-innovation%2Fgrants%2Feha-grants-hall-of-fame%2F2025-winners\", \"text\": \"facebook\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 3934, \"end\": 4114, \"text\": \"rs\\nLeft Sidebar\\n11 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\n2023 winners\\n2024 winners\\n2025 winners\\nPrevious winners, 2012–2022\\n2026 winners\\n2025 winners\\nJun\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-7ad170c3c8cf26dee84e0e4f\", \"title\": \"Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3922, \"end\": 3948, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 26}, {\"start\": 4003, \"end\": 5577, \"excerpt_start\": 27, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Specialized Working Groups\\nEHA’s Specialized Working Groups (SWGs) foster science and spread knowledge in basic, translational, and clinical research in hematology.\\nTo ensure we cover the full field of hematology and provide a research platform for all groups and researchers, we’ve established two types of SWG:\\nDisease-oriented SWGs—which cover specific topics such as leukemias and lymphomas\\nOverarching SWGs—which cover broad themes such as aging and precision medicine\\nThis model is based on the nine sections of the EHA Roadmap for European Hematology Research.\\nThere are currently 25 SWGs. You can use the filter below to view them by type.\\nHow to join an SWG\\nIf you’re interested in making new connections or sharing your expertise, you can apply to join an SWG. To do this, just follow the instructions on the main page of the relevant SWG.\\nSWG Grants\\nEHA provides financial support to small research projects initiated by our SWGs. You can find out more about his support, and discover some of the projects we’ve already supported, in the SWG Grants section.\\nEHA Lymphoma Group\\nEuropean Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC)\\nEuropean Scientific foundation for Laboratory Hemato Oncology (ESLHO)\\nOverarching Specialized Working Group on Diagnostics in Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Acute Myeloid Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adolescents and Young Adults with Hematologic Diseases (AYA)\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Aging and Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Bleeding and Thrombosis\\nSpecialized Working Grou\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"title\": \"Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3902, \"end\": 4532, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 630}, {\"start\": 4773, \"end\": 4793, \"excerpt_start\": 631, \"excerpt_end\": 651}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nHemaSphere\\nGrants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-82ed4576ec5ac8372f114a9b\", \"title\": \"EHA2027 Congress - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA2027 Congress - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3882, \"end\": 5254, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1372}, {\"start\": 5495, \"end\": 5515, \"excerpt_start\": 1373, \"excerpt_end\": 1393}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA2027 Congress\\nShape the future of hematology\\nJune 10–13, 2027\\n| Barcelona, Spain\\nLet’s meet at EHA2027, where we connect the global hematology community.\\nEHA2027 will once again offer an exceptional scientific program, featuring a seamless flow of engagement across plenary sessions—including the opening ceremony, plenary abstracts session, and presidential sessions—alongside carefully curated sponsored sessions spread throughout each Congress day.\\nWith a comprehensive program and two poster sessions, we look forward to sharing the latest clinical and research updates in hematology with you.\\nEHA2027 is intended for medical professionals, national hematology societies, patient advocates, medical industry, and media worldwide.\\nThe Congress is not open to the general public.\\nPatient advocates are welcome to attend scientific sessions.\\nKey Dates\\nMarch 1, 2027\\nAbstract submission deadline\\nGrant application deadline\\nMay 3, 2027\\nEarly registration deadline\\nMay 6, 2027\\nLate-breaking abstract submission deadline\\nJune 10-13, 2027\\nEHA2027 Congress in Barcelona, Spain\\nLatest information on EHA2027\\nEHA2027 registration\\nEHA2027 program\\nEHA2027 abstract submission\\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\\nEHA2027 sustainability\\nCongress Archive\\nEHA2026 Congress Library\\nFuture Congresses\\nSponsor EHA2027\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4010, \"end\": 5610, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEuropean affairs\\nEHA Campus\\nGrants\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nWhat’s new?\\nGo to overview\\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\\nThursday, July 23, 2026\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\\nMonday, July 6, 2026\\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\\nReady to join our community?\\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\\nJoin EHA today\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nBecome a mentor today\\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to suppo\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-1b2e3ae206bf6a7d30e47fb6\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3842, \"end\": 4875, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1033}, {\"start\": 5116, \"end\": 5136, \"excerpt_start\": 1034, \"excerpt_end\": 1054}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Grants\\nEHA’s foundations are built upon our belief that it’s the collective endeavors of our community—in research and clinical practice—that lead to exponential advancements.\\nWe’re committed to accelerating progress in hematology by promoting collaboration, education, and research across all levels.\\nAn important way of achieving this is through the careful and selective allocation of grants and funding to aspiring scientists and researchers.\\nTo check which of our grants you can apply for, use the filters below. Alternatively, you can read about our different grant categories:\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nIn this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-b34424f0bb7a7d0dc0752cfc\", \"title\": \"Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3910, \"end\": 4832, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 922}, {\"start\": 5073, \"end\": 5093, \"excerpt_start\": 923, \"excerpt_end\": 943}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Topics-in-Focus program\\nSupport for a changing world.\\nWith advancements in medical technology and research, there’s never been a more exciting time to be involved in hematology.\\nAs pioneers in our field, our role is to lead the change and find novel ways to incorporate new techniques and therapies into daily practice. We need to rapidly deploy these innovations to fuel our advance towards prevention, a cure, and improved quality of life.\\nOverview\\nEHA launched the Topics-in-Focus program to provide support and guidance to hematologists and amplify efforts by focusing on a specific disease related or area related topics to provide better access to innovation.\\nThe program is designed to:\\nRaise awareness\\nProvide education\\nDevelop further research frameworks and access\\nBuild a network of experts in specific focus areas\\nThe program has two strands, each with a specific theme:\\nPrecision hematology\\nHemoglobinopathies\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-cadb8bc3ab6b0c81b9da0eab\", \"title\": \"2025 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)2025 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3937, \"end\": 3993, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 56}, {\"start\": 4098, \"end\": 5642, \"excerpt_start\": 57, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n11 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\n2025 winners\\nJunior Research Grant\\nMaria Jassinskaja, Lund University, Sweden\\nTopic: Rejuvenating aged hematopoiesis via modulation of the bone marrow niche\\nVanessa Katia Favasuli, Candiolo Cancer Institute, Fondazione del Piemonte per l’Oncologia, Italy\\nTopic: Decoding the biologic and therapeutic roles of lncRNAs in multiple myeloma\\nSrdjan Grusanovic, Institute of Molecular Genetics of the Czech Academy of Sciences, Czechia\\nTopic: Effects of chronic inflammation on hematopoietic stem cell aging and response to infection\\nAdvanced Research Grant\\nNisha Narayan, University of Cambridge, United Kingdom\\nTopic: Clonal tracing to assess leukaemia stem cell heterogeneity and mechanisms of therapy resistance in acute myeloid leukaemia\\nAnastasia Conti, Fondazione Telethon ETS, Italy\\nTopic: Transposable element reactivation in Acute Myeloid Leukemia: functional relevance to therapy response and relapse\\nHeidi Neubauer, University of Veterinary Medicine Vienna, Austria\\nTopic: The mechanisms of STAT5B sex-specific functions in hematopoiesis\\nPhysician Scientist Research Grant\\nAnjum Khan, University of York, United Kingdom\\nTopic: Targeting proteostatic vulnerabilities in leukaemic stem cells\\nAnjali Cremer, Goethe University Hospital Frankfurt, Germany\\nTopic: Mechanisms of response and resistance to CD38 blocking in adult R/R T-ALL\\nTomas Jelinek, University of Ostrava, Czechia\\nTopic: Tumor microenvironment and clonal evolution in myeloma extramedullary disease\\nTopics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant\\nMegane Brusson, Imagine Institute, \"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"web-1b2e3ae206bf6a7d30e47fb6\", \"web-1e06c10fa8edbbfd5a34f082\", \"web-2681df3d0c7c018f4be24234\", \"web-cadb8bc3ab6b0c81b9da0eab\", \"web-82ed4576ec5ac8372f114a9b\", \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"web-b34424f0bb7a7d0dc0752cfc\", \"web-7ad170c3c8cf26dee84e0e4f\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-1b2e3ae206bf6a7d30e47fb6\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (E